1
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for a certain day
floating on the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:24,660
I kicked a pebble and my shoe flew off too.

3
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:32,860
onto the head of a carpenter
who had been saving his money,

4
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:39,120
they laughed that I'm still just a kid.

5
00:00:39,870 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I chase after some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
Katsushika, the same as ever,
one yawn, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,160
The streetscape is strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,120
From the pointed hat and the water basin,

9
00:01:01,740 --> 00:01:07,440
the sunset sinks toward Taishakuten.

10
00:01:10,980 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow will end just like this, too

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,060
Katsushika, Shibamata,
losing happiness once again,

12
00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:24,620
because I'm a fool who
only just realized it.

13
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:52,760
Ryo-chan, why don't you eat
something different once in a while?

14
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:54,385
Something different like what?

15
00:01:54,435 --> 00:01:58,100
Around here, there's only soba or the bento shop,
that's about it.

16
00:01:58,100 --> 00:02:01,507
You need to think about
eating a more balanced diet,

17
00:02:01,557 --> 00:02:05,360
or you'll ruin your health eating
that stuff every single day.

18
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:07,200
Hey, put this up for me.

19
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:09,960
I'm starving.

20
00:02:14,220 --> 00:02:15,920
Hey, red car, hurry up and go!

21
00:02:21,060 --> 00:02:22,220
What the hell are you doing, you idiot!

22
00:02:22,220 --> 00:02:23,120
Don't do that again, you hear me!

23
00:02:24,580 --> 00:02:26,160
Such terrible driving too,

24
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:27,900
let's be a little more careful.

25
00:02:27,900 --> 00:02:28,880
Wait, wait!

26
00:02:28,880 --> 00:02:30,980
Anyone who drives like this

27
00:02:30,980 --> 00:02:32,420
No way...

28
00:02:32,420 --> 00:02:34,200
But it's not staged, you know.

29
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:35,140
Someone else...

30
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:40,600
Just as I thought.

31
00:02:56,500 --> 00:02:58,600
Long time no see, you poor fools.

32
00:02:59,860 --> 00:03:01,080
Forget them, forget them.

33
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:01,500
Look.

34
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:05,400
It's Reiji Shiratori.
Don't tell me you forgot.

35
00:03:06,260 --> 00:03:08,040
And I was finally starting to forget.

36
00:03:08,040 --> 00:03:11,760
Weren't you supposed to be disowned
and turned into a super-poor man?

37
00:03:11,760 --> 00:03:14,860
Right. So why are you
riding around in a Ferrari?

38
00:03:15,340 --> 00:03:16,360
Tsk, tsk, tsk.

39
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:20,900
The heir to Shiratori Iron Works couldn't stay disowned forever,
could he?

40
00:03:20,900 --> 00:03:23,120
I did cry and apologize to my old man,
you know?

41
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:25,080
Shut up!

42
00:03:25,460 --> 00:03:26,720
Looks like I hit a nerve

43
00:03:27,820 --> 00:03:28,330
Yeah,

44
00:03:28,380 --> 00:03:33,420
anyway, this Reiji Shiratori is once
again sending his super-rich greetings!

45
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:34,200
Whoa!

46
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:35,860
Pick it up, you poor peasants!

47
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:37,940
Whoa! Money! I'm taking it all!

48
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:42,220
What's this? It's just a toy!

49
00:03:42,740 --> 00:03:43,980
Hahahaha!

50
00:03:43,980 --> 00:03:47,340
Super-rich people only carry cards,
you know.

51
00:03:47,340 --> 00:03:48,020
Damn it!

52
00:03:48,580 --> 00:03:51,720
How did you manage to drive this
without making it play a tune?

53
00:03:52,180 --> 00:03:53,300
Mm-mm-mm!

54
00:03:53,300 --> 00:03:55,200
Ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!

55
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:57,860
Did you suddenly get
rich again and go stupid?

56
00:03:58,700 --> 00:04:00,980
Super-poor bum!

57
00:04:01,340 --> 00:04:01,760
Ugh!

58
00:04:02,020 --> 00:04:04,540
Thanks for the freebie!

59
00:04:04,640 --> 00:04:05,920
I fell for it again.

60
00:04:06,320 --> 00:04:06,980
Damn it!

61
00:04:07,300 --> 00:04:09,960
When I see money, I instinctively grab it.

62
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:13,720
Listen, don't be surprised. Look!

63
00:04:15,840 --> 00:04:18,580
It's an automatic,
and it's right-hand drive too.

64
00:04:19,020 --> 00:04:22,160
So this is a replica based on a Japanese car

65
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:26,300
No, the body and paint look
authentic no matter how you look at it.

66
00:04:26,300 --> 00:04:30,520
They modified it specially?
No wonder it doesn't stall.

67
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:34,620
I had the manufacturer
modify it specially for me.

68
00:04:34,620 --> 00:04:37,240
It fears no hill, no matter how steep.

69
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:41,780
This is exactly why Japanese people
get looked down on by foreigners.

70
00:04:41,780 --> 00:04:42,360
Yeah, I guess so.

71
00:04:44,360 --> 00:04:45,460
Hey, look at this.

72
00:04:45,460 --> 00:04:47,480
It's a wide-body pole!

73
00:04:47,480 --> 00:04:48,420
What is this thing?

74
00:04:48,420 --> 00:04:52,440
You don't know? It's on luxury cars like limousines,
you know.

75
00:04:52,960 --> 00:04:56,720
Using this pole as a marker, you can
squeeze past and turn right up to the edge.

76
00:04:56,720 --> 00:04:59,020
It's a marker so you don't scrape the car.

77
00:04:59,420 --> 00:05:01,700
Usually they put these on sedans, though.

78
00:05:02,060 --> 00:05:04,200
I doubt there are any sports cars with one.

79
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:05,000
Shut up.

80
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:09,340
You're the only one in the whole
world who drives an F40 with this on it!

81
00:05:09,340 --> 00:05:10,840
So what? What's wrong with it?

82
00:05:11,220 --> 00:05:12,900
It's embarrassing,
so just fall over already.

83
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:15,460
Seriously,
it's so uncool it'd make you want to die.

84
00:05:15,460 --> 00:05:17,020
It's not a question of looks.

85
00:05:17,020 --> 00:05:20,280
Idiot, a sports car's
essence is how good it looks!

86
00:05:20,280 --> 00:05:22,360
That's the most important thing!

87
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:23,260
Hmph.

88
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:34,880
With this,
we can drive to the ends of the earth.

89
00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:37,660
Come on, Reiko-san, let's go on a date.

90
00:05:39,340 --> 00:05:41,120
Your work hours are over by now, right?

91
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:42,600
They're not over yet.

92
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:44,960
Then how about having dinner together?

93
00:05:45,440 --> 00:05:46,880
You never learn, do you?

94
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:49,180
After what happened to
you the other day, too.

95
00:05:49,180 --> 00:05:50,740
Not at all.

96
00:05:50,740 --> 00:05:53,440
Our company exists thanks to Akimoto Trading,
after all.

97
00:05:54,300 --> 00:05:57,520
I've booked a table at the new
restaurant that just opened in Odaiba.

98
00:05:58,020 --> 00:06:01,460
A real French chef will serve
you the finest French cuisine.

99
00:06:02,740 --> 00:06:04,180
No, I'm fine. No thank you.

100
00:06:04,620 --> 00:06:08,320
Is that so?
If you're this happy, I'm glad too.

101
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:10,080
I've told you I don't want to, haven't I?

102
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:13,800
If you're going to eat, take me along.
I'm starving!

103
00:06:14,200 --> 00:06:15,640
That's not a place for the likes of you.

104
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:18,620
Here, use this to order
delivery ramen or something.

105
00:06:18,620 --> 00:06:21,100
You can't order ramen with that much.

106
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:36,000
Damn it,
this is why I hate the old downtown.

107
00:06:36,420 --> 00:06:38,340
Go with him, Reiko.

108
00:06:38,340 --> 00:06:41,120
I'm hungry. I want to eat French food.

109
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:44,240
If Ryo-chan's coming too,
I guess that's fine.

110
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:45,360
Take us along!

111
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:49,480
But how are we supposed to fit?
It's a two-seater!

112
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:52,100
If we do it this way,
I can fit three of us, can't I?

113
00:06:53,380 --> 00:06:54,720
Alright, let's head out.

114
00:06:56,540 --> 00:06:57,660
What are you crouching down for?

115
00:06:57,660 --> 00:07:00,640
It's your own fault for
sitting in a place like that.

116
00:07:02,720 --> 00:07:05,040
Even with an automatic,
it's still a Ferrari, I'll give it that.

117
00:07:07,320 --> 00:07:10,020
Well then, Reiko,
I'll take you straight to Odaiba.

118
00:07:10,020 --> 00:07:12,200
With a Ferrari, it'll be over in no time.

119
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:12,960
Oh my.

120
00:07:14,340 --> 00:07:17,380
This is the latest car navigation
system sold by Shiratori Iron Works.

121
00:07:17,380 --> 00:07:19,760
For an ironworks company,
it's surprisingly not clunky at all.

122
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:22,820
If you dabble in too many things,
you'll go under eventually.

123
00:07:22,820 --> 00:07:23,860
Shut up.

124
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:26,900
Where should I set the destination?

125
00:07:26,900 --> 00:07:28,540
Ahahaha!

126
00:07:28,540 --> 00:07:30,520
See? It's a talking navigation system!

127
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:31,660
Surprised?

128
00:07:32,100 --> 00:07:33,600
Hah, that's not rare at all.

129
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:36,240
Nakagawa's car has one too.

130
00:07:37,020 --> 00:07:38,980
It talks in all kinds of voices, doesn't it?

131
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:41,600
Isn't this the same as Kei-chan's?

132
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:44,960
Your company just copied the idea,
didn't it?

133
00:07:45,340 --> 00:07:49,260
Shut up! Our car navigation is
nothing like those ordinary ones.

134
00:07:49,260 --> 00:07:52,000
Fully attentive service version, set on.

135
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:55,080
Master, where would you like to go?

136
00:07:55,880 --> 00:07:57,660
Take us to Odaiba.

137
00:07:58,080 --> 00:08:01,300
Odaiba, certainly. Understood, Master.

138
00:08:01,900 --> 00:08:04,140
Muahahaha! Are you surprised?

139
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:07,560
Equipped with the latest AI
and voice recognition technology,

140
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:09,300
it's a groundbreaking car navigation system!

141
00:08:09,680 --> 00:08:10,360
Really?

142
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:12,860
It's not much different from Kei-chan's.

143
00:08:12,860 --> 00:08:13,440
Hey.

144
00:08:20,980 --> 00:08:23,740
Why is there traffic jam
even though you're here?

145
00:08:23,740 --> 00:08:25,280
Ugh, shut up!

146
00:08:25,700 --> 00:08:26,940
Hey, do something about it!

147
00:08:26,940 --> 00:08:28,200
Yes, master.

148
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:29,860
Avoiding the traffic jam now.

149
00:08:29,860 --> 00:08:32,200
Please turn left at the next intersection.

150
00:08:34,300 --> 00:08:35,940
Hey, that's dangerous, you bastard!

151
00:08:37,140 --> 00:08:38,340
Hey, you'd better not go this way!

152
00:08:39,040 --> 00:08:41,200
It's the navigation system's instruction.
It must be a shortcut!

153
00:08:41,460 --> 00:08:43,380
It's a shortcut, all right, but...

154
00:08:43,380 --> 00:08:45,140
Wait, isn't this road...

155
00:08:50,940 --> 00:08:52,240
I told you so...

156
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:55,880
Even your boasted car navigation
couldn't check for road construction

157
00:08:55,880 --> 00:08:58,560
Come on,
back up quickly and take another road!

158
00:08:59,180 --> 00:08:59,900
No way, I refuse!

159
00:09:00,440 --> 00:09:03,420
I'm bad at reversing!
I'm going by the navigation!

160
00:09:04,140 --> 00:09:04,620
Stop it!

161
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:10,640
Don't be reckless!

162
00:09:11,040 --> 00:09:13,320
Hah, see? We made it through just fine!

163
00:09:13,600 --> 00:09:14,600
Don't be reckless!

164
00:09:15,220 --> 00:09:17,960
Please turn right at
the next corner, master.

165
00:09:18,680 --> 00:09:20,200
You're still scraping it,
you're still scraping it!

166
00:09:20,880 --> 00:09:22,280
Move further to the left!

167
00:09:23,140 --> 00:09:24,960
Now you're scraping this side!

168
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:27,040
That's why I hate the old downtown streets!

169
00:09:27,480 --> 00:09:30,280
Don't blame the downtown
streets for your bad driving!

170
00:09:35,260 --> 00:09:37,520
Master, continue straight ahead.

171
00:09:41,680 --> 00:09:43,520
Hey, why aren't we
getting on the expressway?

172
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:45,480
There was an entrance just now.

173
00:09:46,140 --> 00:09:46,840
Really?

174
00:09:47,300 --> 00:09:50,060
There must be a shortcut entrance somewhere.

175
00:09:50,060 --> 00:09:53,140
Our navigation system would
never take the wrong route.

176
00:09:53,540 --> 00:09:54,140
Don't lie.

177
00:09:55,640 --> 00:09:59,840
You're scared of getting on the expressway,
so you ordered it to avoid the highway, didn't you?

178
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:00,160
Gulp.

179
00:10:00,860 --> 00:10:03,100
So you're planning to keep taking
the lower roads the whole way?

180
00:10:04,140 --> 00:10:05,520
It'll take quite a while, you know.

181
00:10:05,520 --> 00:10:08,560
Is that so? That's strange.

182
00:10:08,560 --> 00:10:09,940
Maybe the navigation system is broken.

183
00:10:10,900 --> 00:10:13,020
I ran a self-diagnostic test,

184
00:10:13,020 --> 00:10:14,580
and there are no abnormalities anywhere.

185
00:10:15,460 --> 00:10:16,580
Jiro!

186
00:10:16,580 --> 00:10:19,100
Get on the expressway, the Shuto Expressway!

187
00:10:20,220 --> 00:10:21,300
Hey, can't you hear me?

188
00:10:21,300 --> 00:10:23,400
What? It's not responding at all.

189
00:10:23,400 --> 00:10:24,720
Well, of course it isn't.

190
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:27,100
It's set to recognize
only its owner's voice.

191
00:10:27,100 --> 00:10:28,460
so that's how it is.

192
00:10:28,460 --> 00:10:30,420
Then you give it the order.

193
00:10:32,800 --> 00:10:37,400
I think I'll change the route settings
to go to Odaiba via the Metropolitan Expressway.

194
00:10:38,160 --> 00:10:39,980
The Metropolitan Expressway, is it?

195
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:40,920
Y-yes, that's right.

196
00:10:41,740 --> 00:10:42,780
Are you sure this is all right?

197
00:10:42,920 --> 00:10:43,920
W-what do you mean?

198
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:47,360
The user level is set to beginner mode.

199
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:50,540
It's been set not to use the expressway,

200
00:10:50,540 --> 00:10:52,440
but would you like to change that?

201
00:10:52,900 --> 00:10:54,840
Don't keep asking me
stupid questions like that!

202
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:04,540
Do you even have a license? Drive properly!

203
00:11:04,540 --> 00:11:06,920
Getting tailgated by a delivery truck

204
00:11:06,920 --> 00:11:09,820
The Metropolitan Expressway
entrance is in 200 meters.

205
00:11:12,420 --> 00:11:13,760
One hundred meters to go.

206
00:11:14,420 --> 00:11:17,260
Hey, are you really okay? You look pale.

207
00:11:17,260 --> 00:11:20,640
You haven't actually ever driven on an expressway,
have you?

208
00:11:22,300 --> 00:11:26,100
Don't worry, I took the expressway
course at driving school.

209
00:11:26,100 --> 00:11:29,300
Mii! Reiko, take over! This guy's no good!

210
00:11:38,140 --> 00:11:40,360
Yes! We got onto the expressway safely.

211
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:42,460
Poor car behind us.

212
00:11:42,460 --> 00:11:43,360
Seriously.

213
00:11:44,320 --> 00:11:46,600
Shibaura Junction in 500 meters.

214
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:49,040
Keep left to enter the Kodaiba Line.

215
00:11:49,040 --> 00:11:50,380
Please change lanes.

216
00:11:51,020 --> 00:11:53,920
Shibaura Junction in 200 meters.

217
00:11:53,920 --> 00:11:55,340
Please change lanes.

218
00:11:55,340 --> 00:11:56,740
Don't just say that out of nowhere.

219
00:11:56,740 --> 00:11:58,040
It's not out of nowhere.

220
00:11:58,040 --> 00:12:00,640
It's been warning us over
and over since earlier.

221
00:12:00,640 --> 00:12:02,760
Come on, change lanes already!

222
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:05,100
But there's a truck coming up behind us.

223
00:12:05,100 --> 00:12:08,200
100 meters left.
Please change lanes quickly.

224
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:10,120
Shut up, I know!

225
00:12:12,140 --> 00:12:14,240
Hurry up, hurry up, master!

226
00:12:14,240 --> 00:12:16,040
Damn it, this is bad, shit!

227
00:12:16,560 --> 00:12:17,540
You idiot!

228
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:19,940
We've passed the exit.

229
00:12:21,500 --> 00:12:22,320
Are you trying to kill us?

230
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:25,520
Any exit will do,
we should get off the expressway.

231
00:12:25,520 --> 00:12:27,480
I'd like to, but...

232
00:12:29,480 --> 00:12:31,160
Move! I'll drive!

233
00:12:31,380 --> 00:12:32,800
Watch out! N-no, stop!

234
00:12:33,120 --> 00:12:35,240
Hey, stop it, Ryo-chan. That's dangerous!

235
00:12:35,540 --> 00:12:38,300
Letting him drive is far more dangerous!

236
00:12:38,520 --> 00:12:39,160
Yes!

237
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:42,620
Nyaraa! Come on, move it, you!

238
00:12:43,680 --> 00:12:46,000
Aah! Hey, Ryo-chan, that's dangerous!

239
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:02,800
Where the hell are we?

240
00:13:03,420 --> 00:13:04,740
We were supposed to be heading to Odaiba,

241
00:13:04,740 --> 00:13:07,620
so why are we driving
down this backwoods road?

242
00:13:08,420 --> 00:13:09,480
How should I know?

243
00:13:09,480 --> 00:13:11,540
It's because you broke
the navigation system.

244
00:13:11,900 --> 00:13:14,440
Blaming others right away isn't good,
you know.

245
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:16,200
But even without the navigation system,

246
00:13:16,200 --> 00:13:18,060
wouldn't we normally not get this lost?

247
00:13:18,600 --> 00:13:19,360
I'm starving.

248
00:13:19,880 --> 00:13:21,520
Isn't there some restaurant around here?

249
00:13:21,920 --> 00:13:22,860
I'm not asking for anything fancy.

250
00:13:22,860 --> 00:13:24,360
Even a ramen shop would do.

251
00:13:24,740 --> 00:13:26,040
Isn't the map a dead end?

252
00:13:26,560 --> 00:13:28,220
We don't have a map,
since we have the navigation system.

253
00:13:30,180 --> 00:13:31,600
The screen's shaking so
much I can't see properly.

254
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:33,400
And on top of that,
the window's gone monochrome.

255
00:13:34,160 --> 00:13:36,000
Can't you drive more quietly?

256
00:13:36,660 --> 00:13:38,760
At least you're better off than
someone with just a video camera.

257
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:40,560
Go left there.

258
00:13:41,900 --> 00:13:44,100
You idiot, why are you turning right?

259
00:13:44,780 --> 00:13:46,000
How am I supposed to do that so suddenly?

260
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:46,820
You're a terrible driver.

261
00:13:47,180 --> 00:13:48,920
Then why don't you drive it yourself?

262
00:13:52,280 --> 00:13:53,340
Which way is the next road?

263
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:54,920
Hey, Shiratori!

264
00:13:59,040 --> 00:14:00,060
How pathetic.

265
00:14:00,060 --> 00:14:03,140
Shut up! Unlike you, I'm delicately built.

266
00:14:05,940 --> 00:14:06,860
This should do the trick.

267
00:14:06,860 --> 00:14:08,360
Alright, let's go then.

268
00:14:11,160 --> 00:14:12,160
Take it, old man.

269
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:14,840
Pipe games aren't really your thing,
are they?

270
00:14:15,300 --> 00:14:16,540
Hey, Ryo-chan, are you okay?

271
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:18,380
Leave it to me.

272
00:14:18,380 --> 00:14:19,920
Tokyo's this way, right?

273
00:14:23,580 --> 00:14:25,840
Outdoors is definitely best in the countryside,
after all.

274
00:14:25,840 --> 00:14:27,040
Really, really.

275
00:14:29,040 --> 00:14:29,580
Whoa!

276
00:14:32,900 --> 00:14:34,600
That was the Ferrari just now, wasn't it?

277
00:14:45,480 --> 00:14:47,680
Hey! Handle it more carefully!

278
00:14:47,940 --> 00:14:49,960
Ryo-chan, slow down a little more!

279
00:14:50,460 --> 00:14:51,500
The car's going to break!

280
00:14:51,700 --> 00:14:53,380
Let go or I'll bite you!

281
00:14:58,980 --> 00:15:01,260
Don't you have a spare battery
or a cigarette lighter connector?

282
00:15:01,420 --> 00:15:02,320
Nothing!

283
00:15:02,800 --> 00:15:04,200
You should at least carry a spare.

284
00:15:04,640 --> 00:15:05,900
What an unprepared guy.

285
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:06,880
How would I know?

286
00:15:07,040 --> 00:15:09,640
Without the car navi, I have no idea at all.

287
00:15:09,640 --> 00:15:11,040
Which way should we go?

288
00:15:15,100 --> 00:15:15,940
It's out of gas.

289
00:15:20,540 --> 00:15:21,980
The engine's not broken.

290
00:15:21,980 --> 00:15:23,340
It's just out of gas.

291
00:15:24,260 --> 00:15:27,720
If things had gone right, we'd have
been eating French food in Odaiba by now

292
00:15:28,820 --> 00:15:29,760
and be on our way back already.

293
00:15:29,760 --> 00:15:32,220
This is what happens when
you tag along with me!

294
00:15:32,660 --> 00:15:34,000
Nothing good ever happens around you.

295
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:35,600
What? It's your fault!

296
00:15:35,920 --> 00:15:37,940
Bring it on, you super pauper!

297
00:15:37,940 --> 00:15:39,820
You super tone-deaf driver!

298
00:15:39,820 --> 00:15:41,280
You two, calm down.

299
00:15:41,280 --> 00:15:43,740
There's no point fighting out here.

300
00:15:44,700 --> 00:15:46,800
Ugh, getting angry only made me hungrier.

301
00:15:47,200 --> 00:15:48,700
This is a real problem.

302
00:15:49,280 --> 00:15:50,920
D-don't worry, Reiko-san.

303
00:15:51,300 --> 00:15:52,880
I'll call JAF right now.

304
00:15:56,260 --> 00:15:57,320
It's me.

305
00:15:58,820 --> 00:16:00,960
Who is this? Don't you know who I am?!

306
00:16:01,440 --> 00:16:04,160
It's Reiji Shiratori!
Shiratori of Shiratori Tekkō!

307
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:06,800
I ran out of gas and I'm stuck.

308
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:08,300
Can you come right away?

309
00:16:08,700 --> 00:16:09,760
Where?

310
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:11,540
Where is this place!

311
00:16:11,740 --> 00:16:14,040
You know where?! If I knew that,
I wouldn't be suffering like this!

312
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:16,200
I don't know where it is, just help me!

313
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:21,020
Hey! It's Reiji Shiratori of Shiratori Tekkō,
you know!

314
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:22,520
You super-broke bastard!

315
00:16:22,780 --> 00:16:23,560
Such an idiot.

316
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:24,340
Damn it!

317
00:16:24,620 --> 00:16:26,420
Anyway, I've gotta get some gas.

318
00:16:45,280 --> 00:16:47,740
No way there's any gas here,
judging by the look of this place.

319
00:16:48,360 --> 00:16:51,540
A place like this is beneath
a super-rich guy like me.

320
00:16:52,020 --> 00:16:53,180
Just go in and take a look.

321
00:16:54,700 --> 00:16:55,020
Hello!

322
00:16:56,200 --> 00:16:57,680
There's quite a lot of stuff here.

323
00:16:59,660 --> 00:17:02,420
Excuse me! Is anyone here?

324
00:17:03,320 --> 00:17:05,700
Coming! Just a moment, please.

325
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:08,680
Watermelon!
They even have Fukuoka City ones.

326
00:17:10,340 --> 00:17:11,780
Poor people's food, this is.

327
00:17:11,780 --> 00:17:14,120
Man, this is good!
Why don't you have some too?

328
00:17:14,540 --> 00:17:16,420
Do you think I'd eat such vulgar stuff?

329
00:17:18,300 --> 00:17:19,640
Your stomach's more honest than you are

330
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:21,360
Yes, welcome!

331
00:17:21,360 --> 00:17:25,320
Excuse me, if you have any gasoline,
we'd like to buy a little.

332
00:17:25,320 --> 00:17:28,180
Well, well, where have you come from, then?

333
00:17:28,180 --> 00:17:29,500
From Tokyo.

334
00:17:29,500 --> 00:17:33,280
Oh my, coming all that way,
what a hardworking young thing.

335
00:17:33,280 --> 00:17:35,040
Granny, this one and this one.

336
00:17:35,040 --> 00:17:38,660
Yes, yes, let me see...
that's 145 yen in total.

337
00:17:40,880 --> 00:17:44,180
Now, what was it you wanted again?

338
00:17:44,180 --> 00:17:46,320
Gasoline, please. Do you have any?

339
00:17:46,840 --> 00:17:48,380
Yes, yes, gasoline.

340
00:17:48,380 --> 00:17:50,360
That's 25 yen, you know.

341
00:17:50,360 --> 00:17:53,320
Here, this'll do.

342
00:17:53,320 --> 00:17:54,520
What's this?

343
00:17:55,320 --> 00:17:57,760
It's a card! A credit card!
Don't you even know what those are?

344
00:17:57,760 --> 00:18:00,920
We've always been cash only here,
nice and simple.

345
00:18:01,320 --> 00:18:04,220
Damn it, you threw it away!

346
00:18:04,220 --> 00:18:05,760
Then how about this one?

347
00:18:05,760 --> 00:18:07,640
It's a Super Gold Million Card!

348
00:18:08,360 --> 00:18:09,500
You could even buy a house with it,
you know.

349
00:18:09,980 --> 00:18:11,140
This thing is useless here.

350
00:18:11,140 --> 00:18:12,820
Hurry up and pay in cash.

351
00:18:13,220 --> 00:18:16,840
I'm super rich,
so I make it a rule never to carry cash.

352
00:18:17,300 --> 00:18:18,280
So what, then?

353
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:21,600
Are you saying you ate the store's
goods without even having any money?

354
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:24,260
That's why I keep telling
you I'll pay by card!

355
00:18:25,440 --> 00:18:27,600
Call the police box,
this is a dine-and-dash!

356
00:18:27,600 --> 00:18:28,120
Hold on a second.

357
00:18:28,120 --> 00:18:32,000
Even a super-rich guy can't beat 25 yen

358
00:18:32,360 --> 00:18:34,640
Granny, I'll pay for this.

359
00:18:35,080 --> 00:18:36,140
R-Reiko-san...

360
00:18:36,660 --> 00:18:38,980
Is that so? Well, that's fine then.

361
00:18:39,420 --> 00:18:41,780
Associating with a guy like this
never leads to anything good.

362
00:18:41,780 --> 00:18:42,640
Exactly.

363
00:18:44,300 --> 00:18:46,980
Granny,
don't you have a smaller TV than this?

364
00:18:47,420 --> 00:18:49,100
This is all we have right now.

365
00:18:49,100 --> 00:18:51,200
Reiko, buy this one too while you're at it.

366
00:18:51,760 --> 00:18:53,180
What are you going to do with a TV?

367
00:18:53,760 --> 00:18:55,020
We're going to hook it up
to the navigation system.

368
00:18:55,460 --> 00:18:57,500
Make Shiratori pay you back for it later.

369
00:18:57,940 --> 00:19:01,060
Thank you for your business.
We haven't sold a TV in ages.

370
00:19:01,060 --> 00:19:03,320
I just hope you have some gasoline.

371
00:19:03,320 --> 00:19:04,980
Gasoline.

372
00:19:04,980 --> 00:19:09,000
Old man, do we have any gasoline? Gasoline?

373
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:13,520
Apparently we don't have gasoline.
All we've got is light oil.

374
00:19:13,520 --> 00:19:15,900
Light oil only runs diesel engines,
you know.

375
00:19:24,420 --> 00:19:26,060
Will this thing really run?

376
00:19:26,060 --> 00:19:28,760
If it doesn't run, we'll just walk.

377
00:19:30,200 --> 00:19:33,560
Isn't it a bit big?
I can only see half the road ahead.

378
00:19:33,560 --> 00:19:36,300
Stop complaining and hurry
up and start the engine.

379
00:19:44,200 --> 00:19:45,520
Yeah, just as expected from a Ferrari!

380
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:52,760
Alright, navigation system on!

381
00:19:53,960 --> 00:19:57,780
Good morning!
Master, where would you like to go today?

382
00:19:58,280 --> 00:19:59,400
Let's turn off the voice!

383
00:20:00,680 --> 00:20:03,600
You idiot!
Why did you go into the mountains again?!

384
00:20:03,740 --> 00:20:04,920
It's fine, this way!

385
00:20:05,140 --> 00:20:07,500
Geez, fine, then go this way!

386
00:20:07,980 --> 00:20:10,060
No, we'd better keep going straight!

387
00:20:10,860 --> 00:20:13,280
No, at this rate,
who knows how far we'll get!

388
00:20:14,200 --> 00:20:15,740
Better that one person runs ahead on foot.

389
00:20:15,740 --> 00:20:16,860
That's true.

390
00:20:17,780 --> 00:20:20,960
Yeah, I was just thinking the same thing!

391
00:20:22,400 --> 00:20:23,820
That slick guy.

392
00:20:23,820 --> 00:20:25,620
That's the forest road right there.

393
00:20:25,620 --> 00:20:26,660
I know.

394
00:20:26,660 --> 00:20:28,220
Not right, left!

395
00:20:28,220 --> 00:20:29,540
Hey, w-what are you doing?

396
00:20:29,540 --> 00:20:30,920
Stop it, Jun.

397
00:20:38,420 --> 00:20:40,140
You went off the road again, didn't you?

398
00:20:40,140 --> 00:20:41,920
We got out to a village, didn't we?

399
00:20:45,440 --> 00:20:47,700
You should have called us from the start.

400
00:20:48,840 --> 00:20:51,160
Trusting this guy's driving was a mistake.

401
00:20:51,160 --> 00:20:54,080
Reiko-san, as an apology,
I'll give you a car as a gift.

402
00:20:55,520 --> 00:20:57,640
Driver, come over here, will you?

403
00:21:05,180 --> 00:21:06,840
This is my regular shop, you know.

404
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:08,640
Hey there.

405
00:21:09,060 --> 00:21:11,440
Welcome, young master Shiratori.

406
00:21:11,440 --> 00:21:14,480
I'm thinking of trading in
the car I bought last week.

407
00:21:18,140 --> 00:21:19,500
You're already replacing it?

408
00:21:19,880 --> 00:21:21,780
I'm super rich, you know.

409
00:21:22,140 --> 00:21:24,360
Rich people change their minds quickly,
you know.

410
00:21:24,740 --> 00:21:25,900
I'm terribly sorry.

411
00:21:25,900 --> 00:21:28,240
Watch your tone when you speak to me.

412
00:21:29,040 --> 00:21:31,540
Find a car that suits her.

413
00:21:34,080 --> 00:21:34,740
She's the one.

414
00:21:35,880 --> 00:21:37,260
How about this one?

415
00:21:37,600 --> 00:21:39,340
Nice. How much is this one?

416
00:21:39,740 --> 00:21:43,300
With the miscellaneous fees included,
this comes to about 290 million yen.

417
00:21:43,300 --> 00:21:44,400
200 million.

418
00:21:45,780 --> 00:21:47,420
I don't like red, you know.

419
00:21:47,420 --> 00:21:48,180
I see.

420
00:21:48,700 --> 00:21:49,740
Priceless is nice.

421
00:21:49,740 --> 00:21:51,440
It's quite a nice color, isn't it.

422
00:21:51,440 --> 00:21:55,220
Hey, you can't just touch things without permission.
Don't you know any manners?

423
00:21:55,860 --> 00:21:58,700
I'm a regular here,
so I got you into the showroom.

424
00:21:58,700 --> 00:22:01,540
You're really out of place here,
you know that?

425
00:22:02,180 --> 00:22:05,920
You probably touched them out of sheer
amazement at all the luxury cars, right?

426
00:22:05,920 --> 00:22:10,060
Besides, these are all cars you
two could never afford anyway.

427
00:22:10,060 --> 00:22:13,360
Hahaha, well, well, Shiratori's toy...

428
00:22:13,360 --> 00:22:15,020
Sub-chief, perfect timing.

429
00:22:15,020 --> 00:22:18,800
Do me a favor and let these two sit in the driver's seats,
as a favor to me.

430
00:22:20,280 --> 00:22:21,540
Well, well, you went to all this trouble.

431
00:22:23,700 --> 00:22:25,000
You know this guy?

432
00:22:25,980 --> 00:22:28,860
I get it, you met through a traffic violation,
didn't you?

433
00:22:28,860 --> 00:22:32,100
No, no, this McLaren F1 is
a brand-new car, isn't it?

434
00:22:32,100 --> 00:22:33,440
Please, take a look.

435
00:22:34,280 --> 00:22:36,900
I was just thinking I'd
like one to use for parts.

436
00:22:37,540 --> 00:22:38,940
This one is top quality, you know.

437
00:22:38,940 --> 00:22:41,320
Hey! You can see these thanks to me!

438
00:22:41,480 --> 00:22:43,580
You! Don't talk directly to the chief!

439
00:22:45,140 --> 00:22:48,340
The chief wouldn't talk to him over my head,
would he?

440
00:22:48,840 --> 00:22:50,060
Hey, Reiji!

441
00:22:50,580 --> 00:22:51,960
Dad!

442
00:22:52,440 --> 00:22:54,320
Didn't expect you to be here too.

443
00:22:54,320 --> 00:22:55,640
What a coincidence.

444
00:22:55,640 --> 00:22:59,700
Actually, I was just showing this
super-poor guy some luxury cars.

445
00:23:00,300 --> 00:23:01,260
Hey, you two!

446
00:23:14,540 --> 00:23:16,180
I'm sorry for the explanation.

447
00:23:16,180 --> 00:23:18,020
That's enough.

448
00:23:18,360 --> 00:23:19,680
Not at all.

449
00:23:19,680 --> 00:23:22,460
Nakano is one of Conterón Ante's companies,
after all.

450
00:23:22,460 --> 00:23:23,680
Come on.

451
00:23:23,680 --> 00:23:27,300
Even if I didn't know, please forgive us.

452
00:23:27,300 --> 00:23:28,420
It's no big deal.

453
00:23:28,420 --> 00:23:30,680
Even the super-rich are hopeless

454
00:23:30,680 --> 00:23:31,520
Really.

455
00:23:33,700 --> 00:23:35,480
This really is the best, after all.

456
00:23:35,480 --> 00:23:38,240
I don't even want to see French food.

457
00:23:38,240 --> 00:23:41,700
Speaking of which,
Shiratori was a bit pitiful, wasn't he?

458
00:23:41,700 --> 00:23:43,080
No, it's his own fault.

459
00:23:44,600 --> 00:23:45,600
Greetings, gentlemen.

460
00:23:46,120 --> 00:23:47,280
You're...

461
00:23:48,180 --> 00:23:51,780
Get impressed again and you'll
be back to being super poor.

462
00:23:57,180 --> 00:24:00,100
Your life really has such
extreme ups and downs.

463
00:24:05,200 --> 00:24:09,500
Wow, I never imagined
I'd end up getting married.

464
00:24:09,500 --> 00:24:12,000
It just happened that way,
but even I'm surprised.

465
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:15,420
Ryo-sama, how old is Maria?

466
00:24:15,420 --> 00:24:17,280
Hehehe, can't wait.

467
00:24:17,280 --> 00:24:20,720
Next time: a passionate romance between Ryo and Maria.
See you then!

468
00:24:30,460 --> 00:24:37,180
People gossip that I'm a
woman who can't fall in love,

469
00:24:37,180 --> 00:24:42,940
but I have mountains of things I want to do.

470
00:24:44,720 --> 00:24:52,020
I want to ride a motorbike
across the vast desert.

471
00:24:52,020 --> 00:24:59,180
I want to be freer than the birds.

472
00:24:59,920 --> 00:25:07,080
A lady's dreams change
as fast as a kaleidoscope.

473
00:25:08,820 --> 00:25:15,080
Sorry, my heart in love, I'll let you lose.

474
00:25:15,080 --> 00:25:22,200
The panoramic future,
its dazzle arrives all too soon.

475
00:25:23,280 --> 00:25:26,439
You understand, don't you?

476
00:25:26,489 --> 00:25:30,100
Sorry, just wait for me.

